  "report": {
    "notes": "Third in the order, after the One-way attack. Six runs: three at 1x, three at 5x, alternating levels (1x, 5x, 1x, 5x, 1x, 5x). Same path on every run: launch at the NW end, climb to 40 m AGL, direct approach at 8 m/s to 50 m short of the camera line, hold 10 s. Use true optical zoom, not digital crop (plan section 7, step 2); lock focus after the preflight; record the configuration snapshot before each run. Report per camera: median and percentile first-confirmed range per level, the difference between levels, and the within-level spread (Appendix C.2). Before the first run: synchronize the PC, camera and telemetry clocks, record the offset with a visible time-marked event, and keep the correction (plan section 7, step 3). Safety: every path stays inside the UAS Fly Area; no path points at the camera site or at GCS-1. The One-way attack aim point sits 60 m short of the cameras. Site datum: the profile origin is the centre of the UAS Fly Area file (lat 35.289972, lon -79.385599, WGS84). Ground elevation 150 m is a planning value; survey it.",
    "dataSources": [
      "Four camera recordings, RTSP main stream, continuous, native resolution, 25 fps, MP4 segments with timestamps",
      "Camera configuration snapshot per run per camera (Appendix B.1 JSON): resolution, fps, FOV, zoom, focus, exposure, time offset",
      "Camera survey record: WGS84 position, lens height, azimuth, tilt, roll, installation photo",
      "Aircraft GCS telemetry log at the maximum rate: GPS time, latitude, longitude, altitude, accuracy",
      "ATOS tag track for the same aircraft (VAL fused), for comparison with the GCS log",
      "Clock synchronization record: PC, camera, video and telemetry offsets with the measured uncertainty",
      "Detection event table per camera: first possible, first confirmed, first identified; frame index, UTC, still image, reviewer",
      "Computed ranges per event: aircraft and camera ENU positions, ground range, slant range, uncertainty, FOV-limited and occluded flags",
      "Environmental record per run: sun position, sky background, cloud, visibility, wind, obstructions",
      "Target-absent recording interval per run (120 s before launch) for the false-detection count",
      "Comparison table: level, run, camera, first possible, confirmed and identified range; level difference with the within-level spread"
    ],
    "truth": {
      "source": "Aircraft GCS telemetry log (GPS time, lat, lon, alt); ATOS tag track as the second source",
      "intervalS": 0.2,
